    {
      "id": 14494,
      "name": "Reverend Pete",
      "username": "Reverend_Pete",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/278dde/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2016-02-12T00:48:18.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Now, I'll be the first to admit that I'm not the greatest Sentinels player in the world. But I know my way around the decks, and have played many times in person and I've played the video game A LOT. &nbsp;Going into a battle, I'm reasonably confident that I'll at least hold my own.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>That said, I've now lost my last THREE battles with Baron Blade! I hit randomize, go in thinking \" well, this won't take too long...\" Only to be surprised by the ill-timed devious disruption, or stinking double backlash fields or what have you. After the second defeat, I chose Blade for a rematch....only to witness Fixer, Expatriette and Absolute Zero allowing the the Baron to pull the moon into the Earth. Sheesh.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Guess you've got my number on this day, Ramonat.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Tomorrow? That's a different story. (I hope!)</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:46:36.032Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
